# Color Psychology Manifest

This manifest defines real-world research sources to guide Codex in assigning emotional, cultural, and narrative meaning to colors. It supports procedural faction design, UI palettes, lighting tones, and psychological resonance of visual elements.

---

## 🧠 Psychological Color Profiles

**Name:** The Psychology of Color in Marketing and Branding\
**Type:** Research Article (Color Theory)\
**URL:** https://www.helpscout.com/blog/psychology-of-color/

Use: Links between specific colors and emotional response — trust (blue), urgency (red), calm (green), luxury (black). Useful for faction tone tuning, narrative alignment, UI themes.

---

## 🎨 Cross-Cultural Color Interpretation

**Name:** Color Symbolism and Cultural Meaning\
**Type:** University Research Guide\
**URL:** https://web.colby.edu/st112a-fall18/2018/10/15/the-meaning-of-color-across-cultures/

Use: Global variation in meaning — e.g., white as purity in West vs mourning in East. Supports multi-faction design and mythic encoding.

---

## 🧬 Biological Color Perception

**Name:** Human Vision and Color Perception (MIT)\
**Type:** Lecture Archive\
**URL:** https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/brain-and-cognitive-sciences/9-35-perception-fall-2014/lecture-videos/lecture-5-color-perception/

Use: Rod/cone bias, wavelength discrimination, ambient adaptation. Influences lighting scenarios, environmental coloration, and stressor effects.

---

## 💻 UI/UX Color Hierarchies

**Name:** Material Design Color Theory\
**Type:** Design Specification\
**URL:** https://m3.material.io/styles/color/the-color-system

Use: Saturation, hue contrast, focus and hierarchy logic. Guides Codex in clean visual prioritization in menus, HUDs, and interface states.

---
